WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
- Hi I'm Gaten Matarazzo.

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:01.923
- I'm Joe Keery.

00:00:01.923 --> 00:00:02.756
- And I'm Maya Hawke.

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:04.790
- And we're going through a
scene from Stranger Things

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.623
on Netflix.

00:00:05.623 --> 00:00:06.660
- Shot by shot.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.410
(dramatic music)

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:15.393
- Okay, clear.

00:00:15.393 --> 00:00:17.090
Clear, come on let's go.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:18.128
- Okay that was close.

00:00:18.128 --> 00:00:18.961
(mouse click)

00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:19.794
- I guess the first thing I remember

00:00:19.794 --> 00:00:20.627
is being squished behind this--

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:21.600
- [Maya] There's no room back there,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.930
and there had to be four people.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.120
- Thank god I got no collar bones

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.854
because I was just like
squished on in there

00:00:25.854 --> 00:00:26.687
(laughter)
like woo!

00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:27.820
(mouse click)
- Too close.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.910
- Relax.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.027
Alright relax, nobody saw--

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:33.586
(announcement)

00:00:33.586 --> 00:00:34.670
(mouse click)
- We're in a warehouse.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.130
- This is a totally built set.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.060
Yeah, this is a warehouse that they have--

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.415
- In a really janky part of town.

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:40.248
(laughter)

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:42.150
- Behind all of these
walls is just plywood,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.740
I mean it really does
look like it was filmed

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.360
on some sort of location
but they built everything

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.193
from the ground up.

00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:48.540
- This next shot I
believe is what we called

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.490
the Scooby-Doo shot.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:50.454
(laughter)
- Yes.

00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:51.287
(mouse click)

00:00:51.287 --> 00:00:52.870
(dramatic music)

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.130
- That also does look pretty Scooby-Doo.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.820
- No this was also Scooby-Doo,
it was like the, (gasp) shot

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.240
- If we are Scooby-Doo, which ones are we?

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.560
- We talked about this right? Priah--

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.760
- I think Priah was--

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.770
- Daphne.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:02.603
I'm Velma--

00:01:02.603 --> 00:01:03.436
- You were Velma, almost.

00:01:03.436 --> 00:01:04.540
- I was Velma? I thought I'd be--

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.430
- I thought it was you were Freddy,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.460
you were Shaggy, I was Velma

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.420
and Priah was Daphne.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.190
- I thought he was
Shaggy and I was Scooby.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.450
- Then who's Freddy? He's gotta be Freddy?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.283
- Why does he have to be Freddy?

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:12.209
- Because he's making a plan.

00:01:12.209 --> 00:01:13.042
- Yeah.

00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:13.875
You're right, you're right.

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:14.708
- Let's split up and look for clues.

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:15.706
- Okay cool.

00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:18.456
(dramatic music)

00:01:22.537 --> 00:01:23.370
(mouse click)

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.203
- I have great memories

00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:25.036
of shooting this stuff.
- Me too.

00:01:25.036 --> 00:01:25.869
- This was like a really fun day.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:26.702
- Really fun day.

00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:27.535
- This was kind of the first
day that we saw all the

00:01:27.535 --> 00:01:28.599
extras also, the Russians.

00:01:28.599 --> 00:01:29.869
- Oh yeah, looks like the Death Star.

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:30.852
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:30.852 --> 00:01:33.066
- We got the first tour
of the lab, it was great.

00:01:33.066 --> 00:01:35.510
(mouse click)

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:36.607
- Look out, Jesus.

00:01:36.607 --> 00:01:37.440
(mouse click)

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.803
- Man, just how cramped
were all of our legs.

00:01:38.803 --> 00:01:39.636
- Oh my god.
- Oh my god.

00:01:39.636 --> 00:01:40.470
- Crouching for a few hours.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.906
- Squats for...

00:01:41.906 --> 00:01:42.739
(mouse click)
- You sure?

00:01:42.739 --> 00:01:44.830
- Positive. The door
was open for a second.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.100
I saw a bunch of lights and
machines and shit in there.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.110
- That could be a
hundred different things.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.260
- I'll take those odds.

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:55.782
(mouse click)

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.615
- Okay, there's the Scooby-Doo shot.

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.320
- Yeah, really a lot of work went into

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.177
making sure all our heads
were in the right place.

00:02:00.177 --> 00:02:02.235
- I went out way farther than it was.

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:04.706
(suspenseful music)

00:02:04.706 --> 00:02:08.220
- Alright. We're gonna move
fast, we're gonna stay low,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.053
okay?

00:02:09.053 --> 00:02:09.886
- Okay.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.830
- How we would ever get away with all this

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.880
is just beyond me.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.420
Because we are very--

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.701
- Obviously crossing
through the center of the--

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.534
(crosstalk)

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.200
- Couldn't get out the
chunk of dialogue we needed

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.033
to get out so we had to keep moving.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.240
- Oh I remember that.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.252
- I mean also this--

00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:24.171
- The sneaking behind the golf cart--

00:02:24.171 --> 00:02:26.080
- - How would we all fit
behind this little thing?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.193
- - And how does that guy not see us?

00:02:28.193 --> 00:02:30.443
(laughter)

00:02:32.681 --> 00:02:33.598
- Let's go.

00:02:37.789 --> 00:02:39.039
- Shh, come on.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.330
- This is George.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.700
- From Russia, him and his family

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.565
joined the circus.

00:02:51.565 --> 00:02:52.461
Actually.

00:02:52.461 --> 00:02:53.510
- That's so true. Nice.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.940
- That was one of the coolest
stories I've ever heard.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.080
- Yeah, he'd had a long family saga right?

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:57.913
- Yeah.

00:02:57.913 --> 00:02:58.746
- But the circus--

00:02:58.746 --> 00:02:59.758
- He was back in Russia,

00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:02.925
and in the 90s they joined the circus.

00:03:05.633 --> 00:03:08.216
- (in Russian)

00:03:09.057 --> 00:03:10.110
- (in Russian)

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:11.100
- (in Russian)

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.729
- I had to work on my
Russian speaking so hard.

00:03:13.729 --> 00:03:14.562
- You're Russian is very good.

00:03:14.562 --> 00:03:15.395
I'm not Russian, but it sounds right.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.563
- [Gaten] It sound very good.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.396
(laughter)
- It sounds alright?

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.410
Well we had the Russian consultant on set

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.350
who couldn't speak English very well.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.560
It was a difficult, yeah.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.240
- George said you did a job with it.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.073
- Oh, that's nice.

00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:25.914
- And if George said you did a good job--

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:28.343
- Then that's probably a
solid, solid thumbs up.

00:03:28.343 --> 00:03:30.926
- (in Russian)

00:03:32.531 --> 00:03:33.820
- (in Russian)

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.918
- I say, "the secret code."

00:03:34.918 --> 00:03:35.846
- [Joe] Yeah the joke is that--

00:03:35.846 --> 00:03:36.860
- And then I separate this out,

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.730
and I separate in into little pieces.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.214
- I know that you end it with, "China?"

00:03:40.214 --> 00:03:41.047
- Yeah, I end with, "China."

00:03:42.213 --> 00:03:44.421
- (in Russian)

00:03:44.421 --> 00:03:47.065
(yells)

00:03:47.065 --> 00:03:48.797
- Oh, I was very hoarse
because of this yelling.

00:03:48.797 --> 00:03:50.820
(yells)

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.903
(grunts)

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.601
(crash)

00:03:57.632 --> 00:03:58.465
- That's not you, is it?

00:03:58.465 --> 00:03:59.298
- No, you did this all yourself.

00:03:59.298 --> 00:04:00.606
- Is that you?

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:01.568
- Yeah.
- What?

00:04:01.568 --> 00:04:02.401
- I did all this stuff, yeah.

00:04:02.401 --> 00:04:03.254
- Yeah, no stunt guy was involved.

00:04:03.254 --> 00:04:04.087
- So fun.

00:04:04.087 --> 00:04:04.952
- But all the stuff that
really needs a stunt guy,

00:04:04.952 --> 00:04:06.573
like George had to get the heavy hits

00:04:06.573 --> 00:04:07.762
and everything like that.

00:04:07.762 --> 00:04:08.990
- George did have to get the
heavy hits. Sorry George.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:09.823
- Sorry George.

00:04:09.823 --> 00:04:10.656
- He was in the circus.

00:04:10.656 --> 00:04:11.489
(mouse click)

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:13.190
(dramatic music)

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.293
(smashing)

00:04:14.293 --> 00:04:16.110
- When I hit him on the head,

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.850
it's a plastic phone
connected to this cord

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.130
and it was made of like foam.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.690
You know you hide the hit and then do it

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.470
in front of his face in
such a way that it looks

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.303
like you're hitting.

00:04:23.303 --> 00:04:24.136
But then the stunt man,

00:04:24.136 --> 00:04:25.830
he's actually hitting
his head on the desk.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.214
And he hits it hard, I mean you can see

00:04:27.214 --> 00:04:28.770
that's not a joke.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.261
That is like a hard, actual hit.

00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:31.094
- That's a hard it.

00:04:31.094 --> 00:04:32.060
- So, ow.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:32.980
But they get paid to do it.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.710
Each time they do it
I think they get paid.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.933
So they're like you wanna do it again?

00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:36.766
(laughter)

00:04:36.766 --> 00:04:37.677
He's like, "Oh yeah, let's
do it one more time."

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.427
Make sure we do it one more time.

00:04:41.317 --> 00:04:42.900
- Dude. You did it!

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:45.538
You won a fight.

00:04:45.538 --> 00:04:46.371
(mouse click)

00:04:46.371 --> 00:04:47.204
You won a fight.

00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:48.037
- Won a fight. Thanks man.

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:48.870
(claps)
Appreciate it.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:49.703
- How long did it take
to choreograph that?

00:04:49.703 --> 00:04:50.838
- We did it on the day I'm pretty sure.

00:04:50.838 --> 00:04:52.510
That was a really fun day.

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:54.191
- That was a tiring day.

00:04:54.191 --> 00:04:55.422
- That was a tiring day.
- Yeah.

00:04:55.422 --> 00:04:56.551
- What are you doing?

00:04:56.551 --> 00:04:57.768
- Getting us our ticket out of here.

00:04:57.768 --> 00:04:59.623
- You want to walk all the way back?

00:04:59.623 --> 00:05:00.854
- Oh no we can hang out for a little bit,

00:05:00.854 --> 00:05:02.222
relax, have a picnic maybe.

00:05:02.222 --> 00:05:04.518
- Have a picnic? We
came here for the radio.

00:05:04.518 --> 00:05:05.953
- [Dustin] If I knew Steve
could knock out a Russian,

00:05:05.953 --> 00:05:09.870
that would've been our
plan in the first place.

00:05:10.933 --> 00:05:11.766
- Oh I remember this.

00:05:11.766 --> 00:05:13.049
- This shot is so beautiful.

00:05:13.049 --> 00:05:15.330
- It's gorgeous, but like I
remember how tired we were.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.265
- [Maya] Thanks guys.

00:05:16.265 --> 00:05:17.098
- Okay last take.

00:05:17.098 --> 00:05:17.931
- One more time.

00:05:17.931 --> 00:05:18.764
- One more time, one
more time, one more time,

00:05:18.764 --> 00:05:19.597
one more time.

00:05:19.597 --> 00:05:20.430
(mouse click)

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.907
Guys. There's something up there.

00:05:22.907 --> 00:05:25.324
(door opens)

00:05:27.061 --> 00:05:27.978
- Let's go.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.500
- What am I thinking about.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.710
I'm looking at a bright blue light.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.043
- How far can I stretch my eyeballs?

00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:38.657
- Because I was doing
it, and they're like,

00:05:38.657 --> 00:05:41.390
"Gaten it's not clear that
you're shocked right now."

00:05:45.023 --> 00:05:46.690
Holy shit.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:50.518
(suspenseful music)

00:05:50.518 --> 00:05:51.351
(mouse click)

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.879
- They had the camera on this drone--

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:54.310
- The entire set is there.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.143
- They just flew it slowly back,

00:05:55.143 --> 00:05:56.140
this is all choreographed.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.751
- [Gaten] And this set is all there.

00:05:57.751 --> 00:05:58.584
The whole chamber.

00:05:58.584 --> 00:05:59.535
- Yeah this is all there,

00:05:59.535 --> 00:06:00.368
this is all real.

00:06:00.368 --> 00:06:01.201
(mouse click)

00:06:01.201 --> 00:06:04.385
(dramatic music)

00:06:04.385 --> 00:06:07.385
(electrical noises)

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.010
- Remember when you saved my life?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:10.843
- Oh when you almost fell--

00:06:10.843 --> 00:06:12.090
- I almost fell off the--

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:12.980
- Where that thing is.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:13.830
- Oh my god.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.290
- There was like gaps in
the thing where the laser

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.123
was supposed to be.

00:06:17.123 --> 00:06:17.956
And she nearly--

00:06:17.956 --> 00:06:19.230
- I took a foot off of it
(Joe whistles)

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.650
And Joe just action-packed hero style just

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.214
grabbed me and pulled me back.

00:06:23.214 --> 00:06:24.460
- You ever so lightly stepped off.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.293
It wasn't like a fall, it was like--

00:06:25.293 --> 00:06:26.677
- It was like about to be that.

00:06:26.677 --> 00:06:29.260
(laser noises)

00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:35.462
- Whoaaa.

00:06:35.462 --> 00:06:36.295
- And that was all a
blue screen right there.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.128
That entire section of wall.

00:06:37.128 --> 00:06:38.618
- No no that was real, they
really shot a big laser.

00:06:38.618 --> 00:06:39.451
(laughter)

00:06:39.451 --> 00:06:40.284
The only thing that's really the effects

00:06:40.284 --> 00:06:41.420
is the laser and then the glass.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.900
And then obviously the big--

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.789
- Obviously the big giant
gash in the universe.

00:06:44.789 --> 00:06:45.636
- The big gate.

00:06:45.636 --> 00:06:47.173
- Very death-starry. Very death-starry.

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:48.006
- Lord of the Rings, Sauron situation.

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:49.684
- It does look like Sauron, yeah.

00:06:49.684 --> 00:06:52.267
(laser noises)

00:06:55.451 --> 00:06:56.970
In the radio room set, you run up there

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.940
and then you just look out
over the rest of the set.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.773
And it's just like--

00:06:59.773 --> 00:07:00.606
- So beautiful.

00:07:00.606 --> 00:07:03.450
- Just plywood stacked
up in this giant castle.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:04.910
- It's just a shell.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.230
- It's just a shell but it's
basically the entire lab.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.700
Looking out over that is really cool,

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:09.730
one of my favorite spots.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.070
- I hope you guys enjoyed going through

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.120
this scene shot-by-shot.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.260
We really enjoyed filming it.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.680
- Check it on, it's out now on Netflix.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:17.189
- Hope you enjoy it.

00:07:17.189 --> 00:07:19.939
(dramatic music)

